ATTRIBUTIONS

OASIS (https://github.com/camel-ai/oasis)
    The social simulation engine DuckDuckGoose runs on, from CAMEL-AI, used
    unmodified as a dependency (camel-oasis 0.2.5 / camel-ai 0.2.78) and
    licensed under Apache License 2.0. OASIS provides the simulated platforms,
    the agent environment, and the round loop. DuckDuckGoose supplies the
    corpus ingestion, entity graph, population builder, agent tiering,
    compiled policies, metrics, reporting, and interface around it.

MiroFish (https://github.com/666ghj/MiroFish)
    The project that prompted this one. MiroFish is an independent wrapper
    around the same OASIS engine, licensed under AGPL-3.0. DuckDuckGoose began
    as an effort to build an English-language tool with a different interface
    and a different approach to agent tiering and corpus grounding.

    DuckDuckGoose is a separate implementation and contains no MiroFish source
    code. An earlier development revision of this repository did carry ported
    code in its ChromaDB memory layer; those five modules and their tests were
    rewritten from scratch in August 2026 so that no part of this project is
    derived from AGPL-3.0 licensed work. Credit for the original idea of
    wrapping OASIS this way belongs to its author.


Other dependencies retain their own licenses. See backend/pyproject.toml and
frontend/package.json for the full list.
